 "poll_sd": 5.39, "poll_weight": 0.46, "fundamentals": {"margin": 9.74, "lean": 3.0, "environment": 7.11, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -0.37}, "rating_margin": 7.7, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.34, "baseline_margin": 5.9, "analyst_adjustment": -1.9, "key_factors": ["Minnesota's Democratic lean and a favorable national environment favor Flanagan", "Recent polls show the race tightening to a dead heat, with heavy outside spending against Flanagan", "Prediction markets still price Flanagan near 90% to win", "Open seat with no incumbent on the ballot"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Democratic margin near 9 points, but recent polls — including a nonpartisan KSTP/SurveyUSA tie — show Tafoya surging into contention, and outside groups have spent heavily against Flanagan. Markets still price Flanagan around 90%, so a margin near 4 points with wide uncertainty balances the tightening polls against Minnesota's structural lean.", "watch": "Whether post-Labor Day polling continues to show Tafoya's momentum or reverts toward the fundamentals-based Democratic edge.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat pits Lieutenant Governor Peggy Flanagan against former sportscaster Michele Tafoya to succeed the retiring Tina Smith. The state leans Democratic by about three points, and most expert raters call the race Likely Democratic, though one rates it a Tossup and another Lean Democratic. Prediction markets price Flanagan's chances around 90 percent.\n\nRecent polling tells a more competitive story: a mid-September KSTP/SurveyUSA survey showed a 42-42 tie after earlier August polling had Flanagan up five, and Republican-sponsored polls have been similarly tight. Outside groups have spent heavily against Flanagan, while Tafoya has campaigned hard on welfare-fraud issues. The forecast lands on a modest Democratic edge with elevated uncertainty, reflecting the gap between fundamentals and the latest surveys.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}]}